## 🟢 What's Working Well

### 1. Clean Technical Architecture
The Astro + Tailwind stack is a strong choice: fully static, fast, SEO-friendly, zero client JS by default. Design tokens via CSS custom properties (`--color-canvas`, `--color-accent`, etc.) are well-structured and maintainable.

### 2. Strong SEO Foundation
- Proper `<title>`, `<meta description>`, Open Graph, Twitter Card tags on every page
- Structured data (JSON-LD) for `Organization`, `WebSite`, `Service`, and `FAQPage`
- Canonical URLs, `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml` — all correctly generated
- Skip-to-content link for accessibility

### 3. Disciplined Messaging Tone
The copy is unusually disciplined for an early-stage business. Phrases like *"No speculative stock language"*, *"Assumptions made explicit"*, and *"Traceability-first checks"* signal seriousness. This is the **right voice** for aviation procurement buyers.

### 4. Component Architecture
Components are small, typed, and reusable (`SectionHeader`, `CapabilityCard`, `ProcessStep`, etc.). The centralized `site.ts` config is excellent for maintainability.

