## 🟠 Design & UX Issues

### 11. Visual Monotony
The site uses the same card pattern (`surface-panel`) everywhere — hero trust panel, proof cards, capability cards, process steps, compliance articles, contact cards, FAQ accordions. Everything is a white rounded rectangle with a subtle border. This creates visual fatigue.

**Recommendation**: Vary the visual treatment — use icons, illustrations, subtle gradients, or alternating background tones to differentiate sections.

### 12. No Imagery Whatsoever
There are **zero images** on the entire site — no aircraft photos, no warehouse shots, no team photos, no part photography. For a physical goods business, this is a glaring omission. Even one hero image of an aircraft engine or a well-organized parts warehouse would dramatically improve first impression.

### 13. FAQ Lacks Expand/Collapse Indicator
The FAQ uses `<details>` elements but hides the default marker (`marker:hidden`) without adding a custom chevron/arrow. Users may not realize these are clickable.

### 14. Footer Is Too Sparse
The footer shows the company name, tagline, location, legal entity, and email. It's missing:
- Footer navigation links
- Copyright year
- Privacy policy link
- Social media links (if any)

