## 🔵 Technical Debt & Nitpicks

### 15. Tailwind v4 with v3-Style Config
You're importing Tailwind CSS v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`, but the `tailwind.config.mjs` file uses v3 config format. Tailwind v4 uses CSS-based configuration (`@theme` directives). The custom color utilities defined manually in `global.css` (`.text-ink`, `.bg-canvas`, etc.) suggest the Tailwind integration isn't fully leveraging v4's features.

### 16. No Error/404 Page
There is no custom 404 page. Lost visitors will see the default Astro/hosting 404, which breaks the brand experience.

### 17. No Analytics
No Google Analytics, Plausible, Fathom, or any analytics tag. You won't know if anyone is visiting, where they come from, or where they drop off.

### 18. No Cookie/Privacy Banner
The privacy page mentions data collection, but there's no cookie consent banner — required in many jurisdictions.

### 19. `functions/` Directory
There's a `functions/` directory (likely a Cloudflare Pages Function for email notifications). This hasn't been reviewed in detail but could be a security surface if it handles form webhooks.

